  h2: The condition
  paragraphs:
    - Limb-girdle muscular dystrophy is not one condition but a group of more than 30, each caused by a change in a different gene. All weaken the muscles of the shoulders and hips first, so that lifting the arms, rising from a chair and climbing stairs become hard.
    - "Symptoms can begin in childhood or in adult life. In India most cases are the recessive forms, in which both parents carry the change: the sarcoglycanopathies, calpainopathy and dysferlinopathy are the subtypes most often found."
